# NAME: Parsec P2P
# AUTHOR: Horatio Xu
# FORMAT: Loon Remote Rule Set
# VERSION: 1.0.0
# UPDATED: 2026-10-08
# POLICY: Choose DIRECT when subscribing.
# PURPOSE: Parsec STUN/NAT traversal and direct UDP P2P streaming.
# IMPORTANT: Place BEFORE Parsec.lsr in Loon rule-set priority.
# REQUIREMENT: On Parsec for Mac, set Network > Client Port to 9000 and restart.
# CAUTION: This matches ALL UDP traffic with local source port 9000, not only Parsec.
# CAUTION: This cannot guarantee a direct P2P path through CGNAT/firewalls.
# NOTE: If Loon is only on an iPhone, its rules do not manage Mac traffic unless
#       the Mac's traffic is actually routed through that Loon instance.

DOMAIN,stun.parsec.app
DOMAIN,stun6.parsec.app
AND,((PROTOCOL,UDP),(SRC-PORT,9000))
